  "reason": "All three completed experiments share the same backbone (scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, multiprofile) and only vary aggregation/fusion, with avgpool+weighted (config_003, acc=0.542) clearly best. The major untested variable is the RNA encoder: we have only tried scgpt. Config_031 (pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) keeps all other settings at their best-known values while swapping in a simpler, high-dimensional PCA representation. This directly tests whether scgpt's learned representation is actually contributing or whether a standard linear projection suffices. If PCA matches or beats scgpt, it frees us to explore other dimensions; if it falls well short, it confirms scgpt is important and we should focus remaining budget on image encoder or profile setting. With 6 experiments left, resolving this core architectural question early maximizes the information gained per experiment."
}

